'''Croakley''' (ケロ助, '''''Kerosuke''''') is a [[:Category:Traitless Enemies|Traitless]] enemy that appears in [[Legend Stages]]. He was added in [[Version 6.3 Update|Version 6.3]].

{{Enemy Info
|name = Croakley
|image = E 355.png
|first appearance = '''SoL''': [[Broadband Omens|Sub-chapter 41 - Broadband Omens]]
|latest appearance = '''ZL:''' [[Forest of Irony|Sub-chapter 9 - Forest of Irony]]
|money drop = 800¢ - 3,160¢
}}

==Enemy==
Croakley is durable, has slow movement speed and a Long Distance attack with expansive reach. His damage is not that strong, but it is guaranteed to [[Slow|slow]] all cats for a minute, which may as well be certain death for units that aren't immune. To compensate for a debuff of this caliber, Croakley has a massive blind spot and his standing range is well within it.

==Strategy==
Treat this enemy like [[Queen B]], but with lower damage and a longer slow. If Croakley is alone, even the weakest of cats can defeat him. If he's paired with a more powerful enemy (like [[The Face]] or [[Berserkory]] in [[Broadband Omens|his debut stage]]), then [[Wave Attack]]s, [[Surge Attack]]s or [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance attacks]] can be used to pick him off from a safe distance. When not protected, most units can simply enter the blind spot without much timing.

DO NOT give units the Resist Slow [[Talents|Talent]] solely to counter him, as Croakley's slow has 100% uptime even against [[:Category:Resist Slow Cats|slow-resistant cats]]. [[:Category:Cats with Slow Immunity|Slow Immunity]], on the other hand, is a very useful asset against him.

