==Trivia==
*His Japanese name, Kerosuke, is a combination of ''kero'', the Japanese onomatopeia for a frog's ribbit, and ''suke'', a common suffix in masculine Japanese names.
*The line, "He's got guts" (ド根性の持ち主) in his Japanese description may be a reference to the manga ''[[wikipedia:The Gutsy Frog|The Gutsy Frog]]'' (ど根性ガエル).
*His Japanese description calls him a ''geko'' (下戸), meaning someone who can't or doesn't like to drink alcohol. The joke is that it sounds like げこっ ''geko'', meaning croak.
**This same joke would later be used as [[Ribbo]]'s Japanese namesake, Gekokku.
*Since the Korean language doesn't distinguish between "L" and "R", Croakley's Korean name, Kelolong (케로롱), can also be taken as "Kerorong", which may be a reference to [[wikia:keroro:Keroro|Keroro]] from ''[[wikipedia: Sgt. Frog|Sgt. Frog]]''.
*Judging by his color scheme, Croakley may be based on the [[wikipedia:Grey foam-nest tree frog|grey foam-nest tree frog]],  [[wikipedia:Common reed frog|common reed frog]], or [[wikipedia:Sandhill frog|sandhill frog]]. His white coloration could also be a reference to the [[wikipedia:Gephyromantis blanci|white Madagascar frog]].
*When he moves, he doesn't actually stay still, instead his sprite moves backwards to make it seem like he is still. This can be seen well if he is slowed. This animation trick is used on various other units that stay still for a bit before moving again, such as [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]].

